# Pin the agent-discovery files to text/plain (#1666).
#
# `_headers` is parsed by Cloudflare Pages and is never served as a static asset.
# Path lines are unindented; header lines are indented beneath them. Both files
# share one block because `_headers` has no globbing.
#
# ⚠ This block only helps if the request reaches header processing. Cloudflare's
# docs contradict themselves on sequencing: the redirects doc says redirects are
# always followed "regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming
# request", while the serving-pages doc says a matching asset wins. `_redirects`
# in this directory is `/* /index.html 200`, so if redirect precedence wins these
# paths get the SPA shell (text/html) and this Content-Type never applies. That
# precedence is settled empirically at deploy time — see the verdict recorded in
# .omo/evidence/1666/llms-precedence-verdict.txt. If the deployed GET returns the
# shell, the fix is a Pages Function (which must set its own Content-Type, since
# `_headers` is documented as not applied to Function responses).
/llms.txt
/llms-full.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8